; flightsquareapp.com — Amazon SES sending records
;
; Import: Cloudflare dashboard -> DNS -> Records -> Import and Export ->
;         "Select file" -> Import records.
;
; Every CNAME below carries `cf_tags=cf-proxied:false`. That is not decoration:
; Cloudflare PROXIES imported records by default, and a proxied DKIM CNAME
; resolves to Cloudflare's address instead of the SES target, so verification
; never completes. The tag is honoured "regardless of the Proxy imported DNS
; records option being selected", which makes the import correct whether or not
; that checkbox is ticked. MX and TXT records cannot be proxied at all, so they
; carry no tag.
;
; Importing ADDS records; it never deletes. If this zone already has a _dmarc
; record, delete the last line below before importing — two DMARC records at
; one name is a misconfiguration, not a merge.
;
; TTL 300 while the identities are being verified; raise it once SES reports
; SUCCESS and nothing here is expected to change again.
;
; Generated 2026-10-07 from the live SES API, us-east-1:
;   dev  102378189980  mail-dev.flightsquareapp.com
;   prod 363434191112  mail.flightsquareapp.com

$ORIGIN flightsquareapp.com.
$TTL 300

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Easy DKIM — prod (363434191112). 2048-bit, tokens issued by SES.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
htixrn3s5pmajwu2w52cyotrjgulmfmz._domainkey.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN CNAME htixrn3s5pmajwu2w52cyotrjgulmfmz.dkim.amazonses.com. ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
fve6oj7anpnzx6zwgtyemxfgusjqxoxn._domainkey.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN CNAME fve6oj7anpnzx6zwgtyemxfgusjqxoxn.dkim.amazonses.com. ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
dqcpyadypwfug5hotuazv6az4d7fvm46._domainkey.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN CNAME dqcpyadypwfug5hotuazv6az4d7fvm46.dkim.amazonses.com. ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Easy DKIM — dev (102378189980). Different tokens for the same domain, which
; is why both accounts coexist without colliding.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
42tm4ulzcppvdcbxhfui2lgcpzzcheq7._domainkey.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN CNAME 42tm4ulzcppvdcbxhfui2lgcpzzcheq7.dkim.amazonses.com. ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
yzgtl7cb2yogzxqqxuauonzcum7ojbn5._domainkey.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN CNAME yzgtl7cb2yogzxqqxuauonzcum7ojbn5.dkim.amazonses.com. ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
xuhutaepffzlnumcdtyduv3sdbf7mwrt._domainkey.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN CNAME xuhutaepffzlnumcdtyduv3sdbf7mwrt.dkim.amazonses.com. ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Custom MAIL FROM — prod. Exactly one MX per MAIL FROM domain: SES fails the
; setup outright if it finds more than one.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mail.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN MX 10 feedback-smtp.us-east-1.amazonses.com.
mail.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN TXT "v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all"

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Custom MAIL FROM — dev.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mail-dev.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN MX 10 feedback-smtp.us-east-1.amazonses.com.
mail-dev.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN TXT "v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all"

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DMARC. p=none observes without affecting delivery — it is how you find out
; that sign-in codes are landing in spam before a member does. Tighten to
; quarantine, then reject, once the reports are clean.
;
; No SPF record at the apex on purpose: SES needs none (DKIM already aligns
; with the From domain), and publishing one here would silently break any other
; mail the domain sends, such as a Workspace or Cloudflare Email Routing setup.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_dmarc.flightsquareapp.com. 300 IN TXT "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:emtuzas@gmail.com"
